1
00:05:20,869 --> 00:05:26,869
Declared illegitimate aged 3. Tried for treason aged 21. Crowned Queen aged 25.

2
00:10:41,739 --> 00:10:47,739
Elizabeth is a drama, history film directed by Shekhar Kapur.

3
00:16:02,608 --> 00:16:08,608
The story of the ascension to the throne and the early reign of Queen Elizabeth the First, the endless attempts by
her council to marry her off, the Catholic hatred of her and her romance with Lord Robert Dudley.

4
00:21:23,478 --> 00:21:29,478
Elizabeth I, played by Cate Blanchett.

5
00:26:44,347 --> 00:26:50,347
Robert Dudley, Earl of Leicester, played by Joseph Fiennes.

6
00:32:05,217 --> 00:32:11,217
Sir Francis Walsingham, played by Geoffrey Rush.

7
00:37:26,086 --> 00:37:32,086
Duke of Norfolk, played by Christopher Eccleston.

8
00:42:46,956 --> 00:42:52,956
The Pope, played by John Gielgud.

9
00:48:07,826 --> 00:48:13,826
Sir William Cecil, played by Richard Attenborough.

10
00:53:28,695 --> 00:53:34,695
Elizabeth is a 1998 British biographical historical drama film
directed by Shekhar Kapur and written by Michael Hirst.

11
00:58:49,565 --> 00:58:55,565
It stars Cate Blanchett as Elizabeth I of England, with Geoffrey Rush, Christopher Eccleston,
Joseph Fiennes, John Gielgud, and Richard Attenborough in supporting roles.

12
01:04:10,434 --> 01:04:16,434
The film is based on the early years of Elizabeth's reign, when she is elevated to the
throne after the death of her half-sister Mary I, who had imprisoned her.

13
01:09:31,304 --> 01:09:37,304
As she establishes herself on the throne, she faces
plots and threats to take her down.

14
01:14:52,173 --> 01:14:58,173
Elizabeth premiered at the 55th Venice International Film Festival on 8 September
1998 and was theatrically released in the United Kingdom on 23 October.

15
01:20:13,043 --> 01:20:19,043
The film became a critical and commercial success.

16
01:25:33,913 --> 01:25:39,913
Reviewers praised Kapur's direction, costume design, production values and most notably Blanchett's titular performance,
bringing her to international recognition, while the film grossed $82 million against its $30 million budget.

17
01:30:54,782 --> 01:31:00,782
The film received three nominations at the 56th Golden Globe Awards, including for
the Best Motion Picture – Drama, with Blanchett winning Best Actress.

18
01:36:15,652 --> 01:36:21,652
It received twelve nominations at the 52nd British Academy Film Awards, winning five
awards, including Outstanding British Film, and Best Actress (for Blanchett).

19
01:41:36,521 --> 01:41:42,521
At the 71st Academy Awards, it received seven nominations, including for Best
Picture and Best Actress (for Blanchett), winning Best Makeup.

20
01:46:57,391 --> 01:47:03,391
In 2007, Blanchett and Rush reprised their roles in Kapur's follow-up film
Elizabeth: The Golden Age, which covers the later part of Elizabeth's reign.

21
01:52:18,260 --> 01:52:24,260
The film explores themes of queen, duke, treason, queen elizabeth i, tudor.

22
01:57:39,130 --> 01:57:45,130
The tone is emotional.
